e of these therapeutics and  people using them under a compassionate  use as well and and I think the  conversation tonight is so important  because I think in this conversation  with President Trump and Martha and  Brett is so important because I think  for the longest time the dominating  question has been you know is it safe to  reopen the economy you know what are the  consequences of reopening the economy we  should also be asking ourselves what are  the consequences of remaining shut and  remain in close particularly when you  look at the economic calamity piling up  when you look at the mental health  aspect of this that even you know one  national hotline alone has seen a 900  percent increase in calls when you look  around the world and 130 million people  could be pushed to the brink of  starvation because of disruptions in the  global supply chain to food and also  because of the corona virus or you look  at you know polling you for small  businesses and a 40 percent could  potentially close their doors forever in  the next six months you look at or even  the health consequences of you know not  essential surgeries and things not being  allowed to take four to go forward  because of the excess as a priority to  the coronavirus so you look at all these  on  consequences of the isolation policies  of the shutdown and as it starts to pile  up we need to be looking at the totality  of the situation as you are making these  decisions moving forward and really  until recently that hasn't happened  exactly right well I I so agree with you  Lee so I said this on Twitter earlier in  the week which is that you know we're  really sick of hearing from all these  leaders about how they're following the  data on keeping the shutdowns going when  they're actually giving us zero data  about the public health costs of keeping  the shutdown going all the things you  just listed we're going to be really  focusing on that on next week's show as  well

